    <description>Tutanota is the world's most secure email service, easy to use and private by design. Sign up for free encrypted email now.

With end-to-end encryption and 2FA, your emails have never been more secure. The built-in encryption guarantees that your mailbox belongs to you: Nobody can decrypt or read your data.

**Please Note**: This is an automatically updated package. If you find it is out of date by more than a day or two, please contact the maintainer(s) and let them know the package is no longer updating correctly.</description>
    <summary>Tutanota is an email client with a strong focus on security and privacy that lets you encrypt emails on all your devices.</summary>
    <releaseNotes># What's new

- app has been renamed to "Tuta" (was: Tuta Mail) [#11153](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11153)
- Drive: basic search [#11344](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11344)
- Drive: show remaining time for transfers [#11114](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11114)
- Drive: show dialog for file name conflicts during upload [#11104](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11104)
- Drive: ask for confirmation when closing the window while there are active transfers [#11174](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11174)
- Drive: retry failed transfers [#11348](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11348)

# Bugfixes and Improvements

- Drive: NaN shown in percentage indicator for empty file transfers [#11103](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11103)
- Drive: improve preselection when renaming files [#11042](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11042)
- Drive: more intuitive context menu handling [#11118](https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/issues/11118)
- Drive: fix rename sometimes not showing up in context menu

# Dependencies

- updated DOMPurify to 3.4.14
- updated undici to 8.10.0
- updated Electron to 44.1.0

# Milestone

https://github.com/tutao/tutanota/milestone/454?closed=1

